#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059505 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059677 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89f65f58-bd3d-5c3f-b9e0-462d74d75b59" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives"}] :question/id #uuid "0bc72287-b782-5add-89ef-f2a465573ab0" :question/math-academy-id "e-3653" :question/problem "Find $f''(x)$ for $f(x) = 2x^3 + \\dfrac 1 x.$" :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(2{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{x})}^{′} \\\\  & ={(2{x}^{3}+{x}^{-1})}^{′} \\\\  & =2(3){x}^{2}-{x}^{-2} \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}-{x}^{-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x) & =(6{x}^{2}-{x}^{-2})^{′} \\\\  & =6(2)x-(-2){x}^{-3} \\\\  & =12x+2{x}^{-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059506 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059678 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6afb4058-908a-5983-9c1e-78ee3fbadf44" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives Using Leibnitz Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "b092bc79-d369-5ff0-a6bb-5fc059699275" :question/math-academy-id "e-3654" :question/problem "Calculate $\\dfrac {\\textrm d^2 y}{\\textrm d x^2}$ for $y = 3 x^4 + 5x+ \\sqrt x.$" :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{4}+5x+\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{4}+5x+{x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =3(4){x}^{3}+5+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =12{x}^{3}+5+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(12{x}^{3}+5+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =12(3){x}^{2}+0+\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}){x}^{-3/2} \\\\  & =36{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-3/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059507 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059679 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "322168bb-52e3-5352-a2e3-c5bdbf2bc13e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Higher Order Derivatives"}] :question/id #uuid "627f1ef4-64a8-5764-89c7-cb4e31009dbe" :question/math-academy-id "e-3655" :question/problem "Given $y = \\dfrac {3 x^2 + x - 1} x$, find $\\dfrac {\\textrm d^{3} y} {\\textrm d x^3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we can rewrite the function as the sum of powers of $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}+x-1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{x}+\\frac{x}{x}-\\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =3x+1-{x}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x+1-{x}^{-1}) \\\\  & =3+0-(-1){x}^{-2} \\\\  & =3+{x}^{-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3+{x}^{-2}) \\\\  & =0+(-2){x}^{-3} \\\\  & =-2{x}^{-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the third derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2{x}^{-3}) \\\\  & =-2(-3){x}^{-4} \\\\  & =6{x}^{-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570709 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059679 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "322168bb-52e3-5352-a2e3-c5bdbf2bc13e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Higher Order Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1612e9ba-4706-5213-9e4d-cb6b22726949" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570167} {:answer/id #uuid "2b069f17-e412-5356-a860-81ca222aa729" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{20}{3{x}^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570195} {:answer/id #uuid "3378bb16-2914-549c-88df-2501f5000303" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3{x}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570215} {:answer/id #uuid "647a3429-1e9b-544a-b9d3-11c5d9d3589c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{20}{{x}^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570300} {:answer/id #uuid "74dab907-e9f0-5710-95ca-4bdd3d7d778f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{x}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "647a3429-1e9b-544a-b9d3-11c5d9d3589c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{20}{{x}^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570300} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6989b96-6453-5959-889b-dc271201d958" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570686}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "224e49e4-5633-5d71-8ad0-69cc905bfd6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-104295" :question/problem "Given $f(x)=\\frac{5-{x}^{4}}{6{x}^{2}},$ find ${f}^{‴}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we can rewrite the function as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{5-{x}^{4}}{6{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6{x}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5}{6{x}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5}{6}{x}^{-2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{-3}-\\frac{x}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{-3}-\\frac{x}{3}) \\\\  & =5{x}^{-4}-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the third derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{‴}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{-4}-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =-20{x}^{-5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{20}{{x}^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570784 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059678 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6afb4058-908a-5983-9c1e-78ee3fbadf44" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives Using Leibnitz Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43acf527-aa43-56a4-a96a-58ef4e28a8e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570241} {:answer/id #uuid "56a0a88f-a8ae-5f65-9f3a-27a2c63d48a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7-8x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570277} {:answer/id #uuid "584a6d9d-1fb0-5bdb-b29c-e22ab95fc9c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-8x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570282} {:answer/id #uuid "73cccaa9-1469-5106-8f3a-4e7dc596b43b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570331} {:answer/id #uuid "feb0e40d-3168-5f79-9621-a08d68c75d15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570576}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73cccaa9-1469-5106-8f3a-4e7dc596b43b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570331} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a4cd441-2d73-575a-8e4f-cf616f00a6cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570647}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f67b31bd-a1c3-55b5-a439-944a03b0aa36" :question/math-academy-id "q-105266" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$ for $y=7x-4{x}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7x-4{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =7-2\\cdot 4x \\\\  & =7-8x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7-8x) \\\\  & =0-8 \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244196 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059677 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89f65f58-bd3d-5c3f-b9e0-462d74d75b59" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a244425-3749-5c1f-8cde-c706ba9401be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241269} {:answer/id #uuid "0f5837e4-11e0-542c-8b9f-939b3ff4674a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241311} {:answer/id #uuid "22ad69eb-6de8-5ec6-8df2-1b4a1903b77e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241480} {:answer/id #uuid "a4e8467a-fb2b-587f-a5f4-a0e51ab08e62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242631} {:answer/id #uuid "f02f5db4-9ff4-5a63-b827-32f454692621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a244425-3749-5c1f-8cde-c706ba9401be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241269} :answer-field/id #uuid "c32d794a-6e85-5bf8-8ed7-81fe7811ab5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243785}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d969ea68-aab7-5811-a686-d14bdbf027ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-10892" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(-2)$ if $f(x)=2{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-7.$" :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(2{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-7)}^{′} &  \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x-0 \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}+8x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x) & ={(6{x}^{2}+8x)}^{′} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 6x+8 \\\\  & =12x+8\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the second derivative at $x=-2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-2) & =12(-2)+8 \\\\  & =-24+8 \\\\  & =-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317331 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059677 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89f65f58-bd3d-5c3f-b9e0-462d74d75b59" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c19f81e-01bc-5afa-9c54-cd5d13905a3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315806}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c19f81e-01bc-5afa-9c54-cd5d13905a3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315806} :answer-field/id #uuid "b556c2a9-a165-5bb4-80fe-96d361886c1d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316973}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6ad0715e-8443-526b-9290-e5e4f91ac239" :question/math-academy-id "q-342851" :question/problem "Find ${g}^{″}(1)$ if $g(x)=-{x}^{3}+4x\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n${g}^{″}(1)=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & ={(-{x}^{3}+4x\\sqrt{x})}^{′} \\\\  & ={(-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{3/2})}^{′} \\\\  & =3(-{x}^{2})+\\frac{3}{2}(4{x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =-3{x}^{2}+6{x}^{1/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{″}(x) & ={(-3{x}^{2}+6{x}^{1/2})}^{′} \\\\  & =2(-3x)+\\frac{1}{2}(6{x}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =-6x+3{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =-6x+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the second derivative at $x=1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{″}(1) & =-6(1)+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1}} \\\\  & =-6+3 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317334 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059678 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6afb4058-908a-5983-9c1e-78ee3fbadf44" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives Using Leibnitz Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74e1d1f8-4b3b-5f18-a100-a8ccb58c59dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315780}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74e1d1f8-4b3b-5f18-a100-a8ccb58c59dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315780} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6b14006-56d1-58f0-b9f3-8c1de5bea365" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317022}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dd8f94da-36ef-5137-94da-7eeaf5cded56" :question/math-academy-id "q-342877" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$ for $y=\\frac{6{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-8}{2x}.$\n\n$\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{6{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-8}{2x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{2}+x-4{x}^{-1}) \\\\  & =6x+1+(-1)(-4{x}^{-2}) \\\\  & =6x+1+4{x}^{-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x+1+4{x}^{-2}) \\\\  & =6+0+(-2)(4{x}^{-3}) \\\\  & =6-\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059679 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "322168bb-52e3-5352-a2e3-c5bdbf2bc13e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Higher Order Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8882614-1542-5cb1-8585-441d502aa822" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8882614-1542-5cb1-8585-441d502aa822" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570504} :answer-field/id #uuid "fae03ebe-384c-56a0-b28b-7e7a4779e500" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570693}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "30675b2a-1249-5c56-916f-1fdddcd8a518" :question/math-academy-id "q-343087" :question/problem "Given $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3x,$ we have\n\n${f}^{‴}(x)=$ \n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3x) \\\\  & =x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3) \\\\  & =1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the third derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{‴}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
